WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
- Well, you've got a film with
Dwayne Johnson next, right?

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:04.240
- [Sarah] Yes. It's a superhero movie.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.590
It's called "Black Adam."

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:06.996
- [Kelly] (gasps) I'm into it.

00:00:06.996 --> 00:00:08.150
- And he plays Black Adam.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:08.983
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:00:08.983 --> 00:00:10.330
- And, you know, I think he was one

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:14.100
of the only ones without the muscle suit.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.660
- [Kelly] Okay.
(audience laughing)

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.670
- He didn't need any help.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:20.000
But yeah, it comes out next July.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:20.833
- That's exciting.

00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:22.910
Have you always want to
do a superhero thing?

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.743
I love superhero stuff.

00:00:23.743 --> 00:00:25.210
- You know? I mean, no.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:26.640
I always wanted to play, like,

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.475
the hooker with a heart
of gold who's like,

00:00:29.475 --> 00:00:30.308
(audience laughing)

00:00:30.308 --> 00:00:31.491
you know, it's like, you know...

00:00:31.491 --> 00:00:33.206
- Why'd she look at me
when she said that, though?

00:00:33.206 --> 00:00:35.456
(laughing)

00:00:37.052 --> 00:00:37.925
- I didn't mean it like that.

00:00:37.925 --> 00:00:40.142
- I mean, I'm a hooker but
no heart of gold, for sure.

00:00:40.142 --> 00:00:41.558
- Ahhh!

00:00:41.558 --> 00:00:42.640
- [Kelly] Yes you do.
- [Sarah] Oh, I Just,

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.740
you know, just like, you know,

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.220
crying and laughing at
the same time, whatever.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.170
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.470
- Juxtaposition of things.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:49.571
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:49.571 --> 00:00:50.404
- That's funny, 'cause
that's how comedians--

00:00:50.404 --> 00:00:52.010
I want to play a serious role.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.410
People never want to see me serious.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.480
- [Sarah] Right, right,
right. Right, yeah.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.313
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:00:56.313 --> 00:00:57.588
- But I-- So, it was
not something I ever--

00:00:57.588 --> 00:00:58.591
(Leslie laughing)

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.180
- No, that's true, though.
That's true. But actually,

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.013
- Kelly was like "oh."

00:01:01.013 --> 00:01:02.250
- [Kelly] No, because you know
why? Why I'm saying that--

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.800
I actually find that comedians
are usually very intelligent,

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.670
very witty, and very deep.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:08.780
So usually, like, this--

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:09.700
- And on every level.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.170
And we have to know every level,

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.640
'cause we perform for different people.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:13.790
Like this audience,

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.030
I would have to know how to
perform for each one of you.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:16.863
So yeah.

00:01:16.863 --> 00:01:19.020
- Exactly, and I actually
think that's why I said, "Oh,"

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.459
'cause I was like,

00:01:20.459 --> 00:01:21.292
"Actually I would love
you in a serious role."

00:01:21.292 --> 00:01:22.125
- Man.

00:01:22.125 --> 00:01:23.507
- Because I think that comedians
do really well in that--

00:01:23.507 --> 00:01:25.173
- They do.
- And I get why you'd want it.

00:01:25.173 --> 00:01:26.620
See, I hate acting, but if
I was going to be an actor,

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.839
I would want to be
Kathy Bates in "Misery".

00:01:28.839 --> 00:01:30.029
- [Leslie] Oh, yeah.
- [Sarah] Right, right.

00:01:30.029 --> 00:01:30.862
- That's a good one.

00:01:30.862 --> 00:01:31.695
- 'Cause no one's seeing it coming.

00:01:31.695 --> 00:01:33.021
- Sledgehammer.

00:01:33.021 --> 00:01:33.854
- I want to play crazy.
- I'd be, yeah. Yeah.

00:01:33.854 --> 00:01:34.687
Just carry it around.

00:01:34.687 --> 00:01:35.680
[Sarah] Yeah, yeah, yeah. Yeah.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.700
- I want to be crazy, and
just in a frigging weird way.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.650
- Yeah, I want to play a serial killer,

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:40.822
or something like that.

00:01:40.822 --> 00:01:42.273
- [Kelly] Yeah! That sounds fun.

